WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:09.618
Hi! What time do you get up? What time does school end? Today we'll read clocks and learn am and pm.

2
00:00:09.768 --> 00:00:14.010
The short hand is the hour hand. It tells the hour.

3
00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:18.594
The long hand is the minute hand. It tells the minutes.

4
00:00:18.744 --> 00:00:23.226
When the minute hand points to 12, it's o'clock, like 3 o'clock.

5
00:00:23.376 --> 00:00:28.938
When it points to 6, it's half past, like half past 3.

6
00:00:29.088 --> 00:00:33.258
Each big space the minute hand moves is 5 minutes.

7
00:00:33.408 --> 00:00:39.186
Count in fives: on 3 is 15 minutes, on 9 is 45 minutes.

8
00:00:39.336 --> 00:00:42.042
From midnight to noon is am.

9
00:00:42.192 --> 00:00:46.410
From noon to midnight is pm.

10
00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:51.042
Watch out! The minute hand on 4 isn't 4 minutes!

11
00:00:51.192 --> 00:00:57.042
Each space is 5 minutes: 5, 10, 15, 20.

12
00:00:57.192 --> 00:01:01.098
On 4, it's 20 minutes.

13
00:01:01.248 --> 00:01:11.994
Your turn! The hour hand is on 7 and the minute hand on 12. What time is it? Pause and think.

14
00:01:12.144 --> 00:01:18.810
Minute hand on 12 means o'clock: 7 o'clock. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:28.506
Another one! The minute hand is on 6. How many minutes? Pause and think.

16
00:01:28.656 --> 00:01:35.250
Count in fives to 6: 30 minutes, half past. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:44.874
Here's another! The minute hand is on 2. How many minutes? Pause and think.

18
00:01:45.024 --> 00:01:50.346
5, 10: 10 minutes. Did you get it right?

19
00:01:50.496 --> 00:02:00.114
Try one more! The minute hand is on 11. How many minutes? Pause and think.

20
00:02:00.264 --> 00:02:07.266
11 fives are 55: 55 minutes. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:07.416 --> 00:02:16.794
Try one more! Getting up at 7 in the morning: am or pm? Pause and think.

22
00:02:16.944 --> 00:02:21.546
Morning is am. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:21.696 --> 00:02:32.274
Try one more! School ends at half past 1 in the afternoon. How do we write it? Pause and think.

24
00:02:32.424 --> 00:02:38.994
Afternoon is pm: 1:30 pm. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:39.144 --> 00:02:49.050
Last one! At 8:25, which number does the minute hand point to? Pause and think.

26
00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:56.298
25 minutes is 5 fives, so it points to 5. Did you get it right?

27
00:02:56.448 --> 00:03:05.010
Remember: the short hand shows the hour; count in fives for the long hand. Morning is am, afternoon is pm.

28
00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:09.857
Look at a clock at home today and say the time!

